@bank all
// Writer 3, batch 10. Everyday chatter for anyone aboard, NOT about work (the user: ship chatter was mostly repairs).
// Food, days off, home and letters, the circles (facts.md 5), seasons, film/quiz/jam nights, the vents and misters,
// sleep, the hot water, Gerald. Neutral in voice; specific in situation by conditions. Bubbles: 60 characters.

== smalltalk
? act:meal
- {dish} again? Good. I like {dish}.
- Is there pudding? There's always pudding.
- Brennan's humming. That means seconds.
- Save me a seat by the window.
- The grab shelf's full. For now.   #funny
? act:breakfast
- Toast first. Then thinking.
- Has anyone seen the good jam?
- Porridge or toast? Both. Obviously.   #funny
? act:dinner
- Smells like {dish}. Smells like a good day.
- Who's taking the last roll? Go on, then.
? time:morning
- Is it morning already? It feels early.
- Slept like a stone. A happy stone.
- The washroom choir's on again.   #funny
? time:evening
- Long day. Good day. Both.
- Tea, a chair, and nothing to fix. Lovely.
? time:night
- Can't sleep. The vents sound like rain.
- Hot water's gone. Character-building time.   #funny
? act:off
- Day off. I've done nothing. Perfect.
- Lie-in, then laundry. Living the dream.   #funny
- Writing letters home. Three pages so far.
- I'm going to read till dinner. Don't stop me.
? act:off weekday:sat|sun
- Weekend at last. I'm not getting up till ten.
- Sunday bread smells. Brennan's at it.
? act:wash
- Hot water's still on! Quick!
- Who's singing? Lovely. Mostly.   #funny
? act:gym
- One more lap. Then biscuits.   #funny
- Vance's name is still top of the board.
? act:leisure
- My Gerald's put out a new spine.   #funny
- Letter from home came. Read it twice.
- The misters are on. Smells like a garden.
? trad:quiz
- Quiz tonight. I know nothing. Count me in.   #funny
? trad:film
- Film night! Not the seat by the speaker.
? trad:jam
- Jam tonight. Someone'll sing the wrong words.   #funny
? trad:observatory-night
- Observatory's open tonight. Wrap up warm.
? trad:running
- Running club tonight. I'm walking it.   #funny
? trad:market
- Swap meet's on. I've brought my old socks.   #funny
? season:sowing
- Sowing. Everything in the garden's tiny.
- New season. New seedling on my sill.
? season:greening
- Greening. The garden smells amazing.
- Everything's green. Even the soup.   #funny
? season:harvest
- Harvest's coming. Brennan's sharpening knives.
- Tomatoes everywhere. I'm not complaining.
? season:lanterns
- Lanterns up. The corridors look cosy.
- Lanterns season. Soup season. Same thing.   #funny

? act:leisure !who:rina
- Tiles later? Not against Rina, mind.   #funny

? time:afternoon
- Afternoon slump. Is it tea time? It's tea time.
- Biscuit o'clock. Nearly.   #funny
? act:off
- Booked a booth for later. Calling home.
- Pressed a flower from the garden today. Shh.
? place:lounge
- Look at those stars through the bow windows.
? place:commons
- New comic on the wall. Someone's in it.   #funny

== rumour
? act:meal
- Heard Brennan's trying a new pudding.
- Word is there's cake on Friday. Don't spread it.   #funny
? act:off
- Heard the post bag's due. Fingers crossed.
- Someone's got a new Gerald. Very small.
?
- Heard the hot water's lasting longer. Lies.   #funny
- They say the knitters are on scarf number nine.
- Heard someone's planning a surprise. Shh.
- Word is the music room's got a new record.
? !who:rina
- Heard someone beat Rina at Tiles. I don't believe it.   #funny
